# 🚀 Taints & Tolerations

## Core Concept

| Feature      | Purpose               |
| ------------ | --------------------- |
| Taint        | Block unwanted pods   |
| Toleration   | Allow special pods    |
| NodeSelector | Simple node selection |
| NodeAffinity | Advanced node rules   |
| PodAffinity  | Keep pods together    |

---

# 🔥 Easy Understanding

## Taint

Applied on node.

Meaning:

> "Do NOT schedule pods here."

Example:

```bash id="4jvhce"
kubectl taint nodes worker-2 app=database:NoSchedule
```

---

## Toleration

Applied on pod.

Meaning:

> "This pod is allowed to run there."

---

# 🏗️ Taint & Toleration Flow

```text id="n2r38x"
Node has taint
        ↓
Scheduler checks pod toleration
        ↓
Match found?
   YES → Pod allowed
   NO  → Pod blocked
```

---

# 📌 Taint Effects

| Effect           | Meaning                 |
| ---------------- | ----------------------- |
| NoSchedule       | Do not schedule         |
| PreferNoSchedule | Try to avoid scheduling |
| NoExecute        | Evict existing pods     |

