# 🎯 Practical Production Scenario

## Infrastructure Setup

| Node     | Purpose                         |
| -------- | ------------------------------- |
| worker-1 | Normal applications             |
| worker-2 | Production backend applications |
| worker-3 | Monitoring stack                |

---

# 🎯 Requirement

We want:

✅ Only backend pods on worker-2
✅ Backend pods only on SSD nodes
✅ Backend pods stay with Redis pods
✅ Other pods blocked

---

# STEP 1 — Label Node

```bash id="ghv2mx"
kubectl label node worker-2 env=prod
kubectl label node worker-2 disktype=ssd
```

---

# STEP 2 — Add Taint

```bash id="5mxyzu"
kubectl taint node worker-2 app=backend:NoSchedule
```

Meaning:

> Only tolerated pods can run here.

---

# STEP 3 — Redis Deployment

```yaml id="xwlwy8"
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment

metadata:
  name: redis

spec:
  replicas: 1

  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: redis

  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: redis

    spec:
      containers:
      - name: redis
        image: redis
```

---

# STEP 4 — Backend Deployment

```yaml id="zb7ln7"
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment

metadata:
  name: backend-app

spec:
  replicas: 2

  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: backend

  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: backend

    spec:

      nodeSelector:
        env: prod

      tolerations:
      - key: "app"
        operator: "Equal"
        value: "backend"
        effect: "NoSchedule"

      affinity:

        nodeAffinity:
          requiredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution:
            nodeSelectorTerms:
            - matchExpressions:
              - key: disktype
                operator: In
                values:
                - ssd

        podAffinity:
          requiredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution:
          - labelSelector:
              matchExpressions:
              - key: app
                operator: In
                values:
                - redis

            topologyKey: "kubernetes.io/hostname"

      containers:
      - name: backend
        image: nginx
```

---

# ✅ What Happens Here?

## 1. Taint + Toleration

Node:

```text id="s8f92d"
app=backend:NoSchedule
```

Pod has matching toleration.

Result:

* ✅ Backend pod allowed
* ❌ Other pods blocked

---

## 2. NodeSelector

```yaml id="vx75kh"
nodeSelector:
  env: prod
```

Scheduler only checks nodes having:

```text id="r48xtm"
env=prod
```

---

## 3. NodeAffinity

```text id="kp0mb0"
disktype=ssd
```

Pod requires SSD nodes.

---

## 4. PodAffinity

Backend pod prefers same node where Redis exists.

```text id="fw4fme"
topologyKey: kubernetes.io/hostname
```

Meaning:

> Same worker node.

---

# 🧠 Important Interview Difference

| Feature          | Meaning          |
| ---------------- | ---------------- |
| Node Affinity    | Pod chooses node |
| Taint/Toleration | Node rejects pod |

