# ☁️ AWS Load Balancer Integration

Kubernetes itself CANNOT create AWS load balancers.

Requires:

## AWS Load Balancer Controller

Responsibilities:

* Watches Ingress resources
* Watches LoadBalancer services
* Calls AWS APIs
* Creates ALB/NLB
* Manages listeners/target groups

---

# 💾 AWS EBS Storage Integration

Kubernetes itself CANNOT create AWS EBS volumes.

Requires:

## Amazon EBS CSI Driver

Responsibilities:

* Watches PVCs
* Calls AWS APIs
* Dynamically provisions EBS
* Attaches/mounts storage

---

# 🏗️ Real Production Architecture

```text id="vlv3l5"
Terraform
    ↓
Provision AWS Infrastructure
    ↓
Install AWS Controllers
    ├── AWS Load Balancer Controller
    └── EBS CSI Driver
    ↓
Controllers watch Kubernetes objects
    ↓
Application manifests use:
    ├── Ingress
    ├── LoadBalancer Services
    └── PersistentVolumeClaims
    ↓
Controllers call AWS APIs dynamically
```

