# 🔐 Terraform Responsibilities

Terraform usually provisions:

| Terraform Creates  | Purpose               |
| ------------------ | --------------------- |
| IAM roles/policies | AWS API access        |
| IRSA/OIDC          | Secure authentication |
| Helm releases      | Install controllers   |
| Security Groups    | Traffic rules         |
| Subnet tags        | ALB discovery         |

---

# 📈 Production Best Practice

Application teams SHOULD NOT:

* Manually create ALB
* Manually create EBS volumes

Instead:

* Applications define Kubernetes manifests
* Controllers automate cloud resources

This is one of Kubernetes’ biggest production advantages.

---

# 🎯 Professional Interview Answer

> Kubernetes is cloud agnostic, so AWS integrations require additional controllers. AWS Load Balancer Controller provisions ALB/NLB resources for Ingress and LoadBalancer services, while the EBS CSI Driver dynamically provisions EBS volumes for PersistentVolumeClaims. These integrations are typically installed using Helm or Terraform and secured using IAM Roles for Service Accounts (IRSA).

